From b6c661279f76309e5f53a2d40be3e7f70fcce56c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 17:39:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] docs: Document the read-back behaviour of the serial MCP tool

Signed-off-by: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
---
diff --git a/main.go b/main.go
index 44e4f8f8cfcc4919fa289cefabb243cde2a640e2..f8e877be774daf8e88940d2d2d959efa8da8294b 100644
--- a/main.go
+++ b/main.go
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ Every partition needs name, offset, size and image. The device builds its GPT from offset and size. Call flash.multiFlash with reboot true when the flash must boot the new system.
 
 Watch a running flash with flash.getJobs. Read status, partition, sentBytes, totalBytes and error.
 
-Start serial buffering before a reset. serial.getConsoles lists the console paths. serial.readFrom returns the captured output. A boot succeeded when the log reaches K3-Buildroot login:.
+Start serial buffering before a reset. serial.getConsoles lists the console paths. serial.readFrom returns the captured output. Every serial call returns only new output, so an empty result means that nothing arrived since the last call.
 
 The KVM path shows the screen. kvm.getVideoCaptureDevices lists the capture path, and kvm.takeScreenshot returns a JPEG. kvm.getInputDevices lists the input path for kvm.sendMouseInput and kvm.pressKeys. A panel launcher needs a doubleClick.
 

